40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I've found some really important stuff! It turns out a lot of our costs are fixed—like hall hire and insurance—regardless of attendance. Also, getting people to pay on time is harder than it looks!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is concerning to see that a small group carries the bulk of the attendance, while others have stopped coming entirely. It seems some members no longer feel a natural sense of belonging.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Takumi,,It's worse than we thought. The same nine people are doing all the heavy lifting—setting up and locking up—while others just coast. It's not fair that the workload is that uneven.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The administrative burden is also significant. I've found that chasing individual session payments takes six times longer than a yearly collection. We must consider the treasurer's workload before deciding on a payment method.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I found something interesting! A lot of people who didn't join or joined late were worried about paying for a whole year at once. It seems like a big upfront cost is scaring people away!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, that matches what I saw in the bank statements! People are struggling with the lump sum. But @Toshio, if chasing payments takes so much time, how do we balance that with making it affordable?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps we should consider a structure that reduces the psychological barrier of a large sum without creating an administrative burden. We must ensure members feel welcome, not hesitant to attend.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, welcome is fine, but fairness is better. We can't just make it easy for the people who barely show up while the same nine people do all the work. We need a system that reflects actual use.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is important, but we must also ensure the system is sustainable. If we choose a structure that is too complex to manage, we risk burning out whoever takes over the books.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"I get that, @Toshio! But if we make it too strict, we might lose the friendly vibe. Maybe there's a way to keep it simple but still let new people join without feeling overwhelmed?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with @Kenji! We need to keep it friendly. But we can't ignore those fixed costs I found. If we make it too flexible, we might not have enough to cover the hall and insurance!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a delicate balance. If we focus too much on the cost or the workload, we might inadvertently alienate those who are already hesitant to return. We should prioritize a sense of stability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"Stability is just another word for keeping things the same, @Jonathan. If we don't address the fact that a few people are doing everything, the people actually running the club will eventually quit. That's not stable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, you are correct that burnout is a risk for the active members. However, the same applies to the treasurer. A system based on high-frequency payments is a recipe for failure. We need a streamlined process.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I see both sides! @Takumi, we can't let the hard workers get tired, but @Toshio is right about the paperwork. Maybe we can find a middle ground that's easy for everyone and doesn't scare off new friends?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! We need a solution that covers our fixed costs and keeps the treasurer sane, but doesn't scare people away. I'm really hoping the options we see next can balance all these tricky points!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I hope so as well. Let us look at the options with a focus on restoring the comfort of our members, ensuring that coming to the club feels like returning home.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I just want a system that doesn't reward laziness. If the options don't address the imbalance between the people doing the work and the people just coasting, then we're just ignoring the real problem.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We must be careful not to overcomplicate the fee structure in an attempt to solve social issues. Let us see the options and prioritize a method that is administratively sustainable for the long term.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm with you all! I just hope we pick something that keeps the club open to everyone. Let's see the options and find the one that makes everyone feel welcome and happy!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
