65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at these, Option A is the safest for our fixed costs, but @Kenji and I know it's a big hurdle for some. Option C sounds like a nightmare for @Toshio's workload! What do you all think?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C seems risky. My findings suggest that adding charges to individual events can make members hesitate to attend, turning a place of belonging into a series of financial decisions. Option A provides the most stability.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is just more of the same. It lets the people who barely show up pay the same as the ones doing all the work. Option B seems better—it actually acknowledges different levels of participation.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, Option B sounds fair in theory, but my research into the minute books shows that named grades caused friction and discouraged participation. Furthermore, Option C is administratively impossible given the hours required to chase payments.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, if Option C is too hard and Option B causes friction, maybe Option A is the way? But I'm worried it'll still scare off new people. Is there any way to make it feel less scary?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, maybe we can't change the option itself, but we can be more flexible with how we collect it? Option A is the only one that guarantees our fixed costs are covered without a paperwork disaster!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Mio. Option A removes the constant weighing of costs before attending. If we want members to feel that the club is truly theirs again, we must remove those small, recurring barriers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, removing barriers for the lazy doesn't help the people actually running the place. Option A is a slap in the face to the nine people doing all the work. Option B is the only one that recognizes effort.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, recognizing effort is a social matter, not a financial one. Using fees to solve it creates administrative chaos and social friction. Option A is the only sustainable choice for the person managing the books.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I see what you mean, @Takumi, but @Toshio is right about the chaos. If Option B makes people feel like they're in different ""classes,"" it might stop them from just drifting in and making friends!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, I hear you, but we can't risk the club's finances! Option A is the only way to be sure we can pay for the hall and insurance without guessing. It's the most stable choice for everyone!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Indeed. When we prioritize the collective stability of the club, we create a space where members can simply exist without hesitation. Option A is the most gentle approach, fostering a sense of permanent belonging.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, ""gentle"" is just another word for ignoring the problem. If we keep Option A, we're telling the hard workers that their effort is worth nothing. I can't support a system that's this unfair.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is not achieved by creating a system that is destined to fail. If the treasurer quits due to burnout, the club ceases to exist for everyone. Option A is the only practical way to ensure continuity.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I really don't want anyone to feel it's unfair, @Takumi, but I'm scared that Option B will make people feel left out. Option A keeps us all together as one big group, which is the best part!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm sorry, @Takumi, but we have to prioritize the club's survival. Option A is the only one that guarantees our fixed costs are covered and keeps the workload manageable. I'm voting for Option A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. To restore the peace and ensure that no member feels a barrier to entry, we must choose the simplest path. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"You're all just choosing the easy way out. If we don't fix the imbalance now, the people actually running this club will just give up. I'm sticking to my guns. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The risk of administrative collapse is too high with the other options. To protect the club's future and the sanity of the treasurer, we must choose the most efficient system. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I want everyone to be happy, but I'm really worried that Option B will make people feel divided. Let's keep it simple and welcoming for everyone! I vote for Option A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
